; A bucket account completes only a transaction that has exactly one
; posting (src/xact.cc, xact_base_t::finalize: "posts.size() == 1").
; The second transaction balances within display precision: its cost,
; 3 x $3.333 = $9.999, leaves $0.001 against $-10.00.  The residual is
; real (kept at full precision in the balance, src/xact.cc:325-333;
; rounded() only clears the keep-precision flag, src/amount.h:351), and
; C++ accepts it because the final balance check (src/xact.cc:898)
; treats a residual that renders as zero at the $ commodity's display
; precision as zero (amount_t::is_zero, src/amount.cc:1374).  The
; bucket receives nothing because the transaction has two postings
; (posts.size() == 1, src/xact.cc:368).  The semantic bisimulation
; (test/semantic/check_all.py) replays this journal, so an oracle that
; completed the residual into the bucket would fail here.

bucket Equity:Bucket

2024/01/01 Opening
    Assets:Cash   $100.00
    Equity:Open  $-100.00

2024/01/02 Buy with rounded cost
    Assets:Broker   3 AAPL @ $3.333
    Assets:Cash     $-10.00

test bal --flat
              3 AAPL  Assets:Broker
              $90.00  Assets:Cash
            $-100.00  Equity:Open
--------------------
             $-10.00
              3 AAPL
end test
